Description: matroskaenc: always write Duration in header
 Stock matroska muxer skips the Duration field in the header when
 `is_live=1`. Plex's segment muxer drives matroskaenc with `live=1`
 (each chunk is a self-contained matroska stream that begins/ends
 without seeking the IO), but Plex clients (Plex for Windows in
 particular — mpv-based) need Duration to position the slider and
 enable seek before the trailing chunks arrive.

 Plex's own ffmpeg fork uses the same short-circuit (`|| 1`) — port
 verbatim. The rest of the is_live semantics (no SeekHead, no Cues)
 stay intact.

 The Duration value comes from `s->duration` (recording time) or
 `get_metadata_duration()` (container metadata). In scaleplex's case,
 PMS sets `-metadata duration=<microseconds>` on the encoder cmdline,
 so metadata_duration is populated and lands in the header.

 Without this patch scaleplex must use `live=0` for matroska-segmented
 output (Plex Windows shape) and compensate via per-frame clusters,
 which produces 14-byte Cluster headers per video frame and bloats
 the chunk stream. With this patch we keep `live=1` + default cluster
 cadence.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/plexinc/plex-media-server-ffmpeg-gpl
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-11
---
--- a/libavformat/matroskaenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/matroskaenc.c
@@ -2570,7 +2570,11 @@ static int mkv_write_info(AVFormatContex
     // reserve space for the duration
     mkv->duration = 0;
     mkv->duration_offset = avio_tell(pb);
-    if (!mkv->is_live) {
+    // scaleplex: always write Duration regardless of is_live. Plex's
+    // Windows desktop client (mpv) reads Duration from the header to
+    // position the slider; without it the slider grows incrementally
+    // and seek-to-position is broken until all chunks arrive.
+    if (!mkv->is_live || 1) {
         int64_t metadata_duration = get_metadata_duration(s);

         if (s->duration > 0) {
